    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9b2d4b47_5614276e",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/IpSecService.java",
        "patchSetId": 28
      },
      "lineNbr": 103,
      "author": {
        "id": 1107893
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-06-27T05:18:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am not a fan of this. Consider instead using a \"config object\" that can be mocked easily:\n\ninterface IpSecServiceConfiguration { // or \"Dependencies\"\n  INetd getNetdInstance() throws RemoteException\n\n  static DEFAULT \u003d new IpSecServiceConfiguration() {\n    @Override\n    public INetd getNetdInstance() throws RemoteException {\n      /* the existing getNetdInstance() modified\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nthen add a local variable IpSecServiceConfiguration mConfig and in the ctor of IpSecService:\n\nprivate IpSecService(Context context) {\n    this(context, IpSecServiceConfiguration.Default);\n}\n\n@VisibleForTesting\nIpSecService(Context context, IpSecServiceConfiguration config) {\n    mContext \u003d context;\n    mConfig \u003d config\n}\n\nthen in test just @Mock the IpSecServiceConfiguration object.\n\nThat config interface can be later grown to have more stuff, which is superior to having to put extra semi-hidden setters just for tests.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 100,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 103,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "299454eead3b8bf17113c10388ccd8ae9855c894",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
